  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: db176a60e3b58b4408636b22a97519c4, type: 3}
  m_Name: HabitatTemperatureDropEvent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MarsEvent
  eventTitle: Habitat Temperature Drop
  eventDescription: Warning! A sudden temperature drop is affecting the Mars outpost.
    The habitat's heating system is struggling to maintain safe internal conditions.
    The crew must decide how to protect themselves from the extreme cold while managing
    the base's limited energy and life support resources.
  targetSol: 8
  optionATitle: Activate Emergency Heating
  energyChangeA: -15
  lifeSupportChangeA: 15
  shieldChangeA: 0
  resultTitleA: Emergency Heating Activated
  resultDescriptionA: The emergency heating system successfully stabilizes the habitat's
    internal temperature. The crew is protected from the extreme cold, improving
    life support conditions. However, maintaining a safe temperature requires a significant
    amount of energy.
  optionBTitle: Reinforce Thermal Insulation
  energyChangeB: -5
  lifeSupportChangeB: 8
  shieldChangeB: -8
  resultTitleB: Thermal Insulation Reinforced
  resultDescriptionB: The crew installs additional thermal insulation to reduce heat
    loss inside the habitat. Internal conditions improve with lower energy consumption,
    but the operation requires materials originally reserved for protective maintenance,
    reducing the base's shield integrity.
  educationalExplanation: Mars has an extremely cold environment, with an average
    surface temperature of approximately -63 degrees Celsius. Its thin atmosphere
    provides limited protection against temperature changes. Future human habitats
    on Mars will require reliable heating systems, thermal insulation, and environmental
    controls to maintain safe living conditions for astronauts.
  scientificSource: "NASA \u2014 Mars Facts"
  scientificSourceURL: https://science.nasa.gov/mars/facts/
